From 246b9d758958b7ad6552a7c8cc304469fcdff9fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 07:18:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add hub_moments & rsp_validation_events (migration, types,
 UI, RPC)

### Motivation

- Provide a backend-backed audit trail and validation flow for live "hub moments" so validated family coordination events produce auditable records and Event Token payloads.
- Surface live validation status in the family hub UI and allow on-demand validation refreshes to keep the client view in sync with backend validation processing.

### Description

- Add a new database migration `supabase/migrations/20260616190000_rsp_validation_events.sql` that creates `hub_moments` and `rsp_validation_events` tables, indexes, RLS policies, and a security-definer function `validate_due_hub_moments` which updates moments, emits validation events, and generates burn receipts and token payloads.
- Extend Supabase TypeScript types in `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` to include the new tables and the `validate_due_hub_moments` RPC signature.
- Update the family hub UI in `src/routes/_authenticated.app.tsx` to fetch and render recent `hub_moments`, add a `Refresh validation` button wired to the `validate_due_hub_moments` RPC via a React Query `useMutation`, and write `hub_moments` when routing support signals to create the validation trail.
- Add explanatory copy in `src/routes/rsp.tsx` describing the backend validation event record and its role as the bridge to Event Token payloads.

### Testing

- Ran TypeScript typecheck with `tsc --noEmit` which completed successfully.
- Performed a production build with the project build script (`pnpm build`) which succeeded.
- Executed the existing automated test suite with `pnpm test` and all tests passed.
